    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-grĕdĭor</span></b> ,
			gressus, grĕdi, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v dep</i> [gradior], <i>to
				go</i> or <i>walk around</i>, <i>travel about</i> (esp. in a hostile manner; post-Aug., several
			times in Tac, elsewhere rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 1, 64, 2, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12,
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With <i>acc.</i>: exercitum, * <i><span class="en">Sall.
				H. 4, 61, 21</span></i> Dietsch: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 25</span></i>
			' Syriam, Aur Vict. <i><span class="en">Caes. 21</span></i>'
			lacunam, <i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 12, 59</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
